2️⃣ Payment Service APIs
API 5 — Process Payment

POST

http://localhost:8082/payments

Body:

{
    "orderId": 1,
    "amount": 50000
}

Response:

{
    "id": 1,
    "orderId": 1,
    "amount": 50000.0,
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}
API 6 — Failed Payment

You can test the failure scenario using:

POST

http://localhost:8082/payments

Body:

{
    "orderId": 2,
    "amount": 0
}

Response:

{
    "id": 2,
    "orderId": 2,
    "amount": 0.0,
    "status": "FAILED"
}

Our simple logic is:

amount > 0  → SUCCESS
amount <= 0 → FAILED
API 7 — Get All Payments

GET

http://localhost:8082/payments

Response:

[
    {
        "id": 1,
        "orderId": 1,
        "amount": 50000.0,
        "status": "SUCCESS"
    },
    {
        "id": 2,
        "orderId": 2,
        "amount": 0.0,
        "status": "FAILED"
    }
]
API 8 — Get Payment By ID

GET

http://localhost:8082/payments/1

Response:

{
    "id": 1,
    "orderId": 1,
    "amount": 50000.0,
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}
API 9 — Refund Payment

This is important for the Saga compensation.

PUT

http://localhost:8082/payments/1/refund

Response:

{
    "id": 1,
    "orderId": 1,
    "amount": 50000.0,
    "status": "REFUNDED"
}
